# ---- South-west: Lockspire Keep, the thieves' testing grounds ----
# Safe route from pawnshop (15) south to 58, west across the causeway.
# Stairwells are always accessible; locked doors lead to optional challenge rooms.
# Lock identifiers are mechanisms, not difficulty scores; trap values escalate.
# No wandering monsters in the keep: focus is on thief skills.

[description 11]
1 = 1/You are on the south-west lane. A ruined keep rises beyond the fields./
2 = 1/You are on the old causeway. The keep stands to the west./
3 = 1/You are at the keep's warning board. The gate is west./
4 = 1/You stand in Lockspire courtyard. Entry to the keep lies west./
5 = 1/You are in the ground-floor entry. Practice corridors lead west./
6 = 1/You are in the novice lock hall. Two doors lead to practice chambers./
7 = 1/You are in the brass-lock chamber. A low chest rests on a bench./
8 = 1/You are in the needle-lock chamber. A chest bears a tiny keyhole./
9 = 1/You are at the first stairwell. Steps climb to the second floor./
10 = 1/You are on the second landing. A corridor runs west./

[description 12]
1 = 1/You are in the warded corridor. Faint holes mark the stonework./
2 = 1/You are in the old records room. Shelves surround a heavy chest./
3 = 1/You are in the armory vault. A steel-bound strongbox waits here./
4 = 1/You are at the second stairwell. Steps climb to the third floor./
5 = 1/You are on the third landing. Fine locks adorn two dark doors./
6 = 1/You are in the master lock hall. Dust outlines hidden trigger plates./
7 = 1/You are in the jewel chamber. A carved chest stands under a lamp./
8 = 1/You are in the artificer's treasury. Complex mechanisms hum softly./
9 = 1/You are at the roof stair. The final flight rises above./
10 = 1/You are on the battlement. The city and Graveward lie below./

[description 13]
1 = 1/You are in the crowning vault. A final chest awaits a master thief./
2 = 1/THIEVES: This keep has locks and traps. Every staircase stays open./
3 = 1/Begin with the first floor. Locks and trap risk rise as you climb./
4 = 1/A battered practice chest with a simple latch and blunt trap pin./
5 = 1/A narrow strongbox with carefully fitted brass mechanisms./
6 = 1/A reinforced coffer with hidden spring needles./
7 = 1/A steel vault chest engraved with winding geometric lines./
8 = 1/A jewel casket with a subtle pressure-release catch./
9 = 1/A masterwork clockwork chest with intricate internal tumblers./
10 = 1/A crown-shaped iron chest surrounded by concealed trigger slots./

